[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a way I can pattern match on a subterm of my goal and then replace the whole subterm with a hypothesis and introduce an equation saying that the hypothesis is equal to the subterm? </p>\n<p>I'm working on a verification project and I am frequently ending up with huge subterms in my goal that I would like to replace with a variable. Right now, I'm working on proving program equivalence which is relatively concise except for a hundred line long subterm containing a string of context renamings. This subterm makes it hard to read the whole goal, and some of the equations I need to apply have the effect of duplicating the whole subterm (by pushing the renaming through operations into their multiple child nodes).</p>\n<p>I know that I can use the change tactic if I write the whole subterm in my proof, but its way to large for this to be practical. I'd like to be able to pattern match on the subterm or use conv to navigate to it as the goal, and then replace it with a variable and an equation.</p>",
        "id": 600131469,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780591048
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You're probably looking for <code>generalize ha : my large subterm = a</code></p>",
        "id": 600150258,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780596990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this still requires the large subterm to be written out</p>",
        "id": 600155235,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780598806
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I misunderstood,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">opaque</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Something</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Something</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">24</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">factorial</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">enter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is an option. I think there was a discussion about something similar some time ago?</p>",
        "id": 600156838,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780599389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it would be nice if we got a solution that always works</p>",
        "id": 600156990,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780599444
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in this case it only works if <code>conv</code> can access the subterm</p>",
        "id": 600157018,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780599454
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The conv solution works well in my case, thank you!</p>",
        "id": 600157764,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780599702
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, generalize also works by pattern matching on the head of the subterm and leaving holes</p>",
        "id": 600158435,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780599961
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And generalize is actually better because it allows me to easily omit the equality hypothesis while working on the rest of the term, keeping my context readable. Then I can introduce it once I need it later.</p>",
        "id": 600158681,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780600047
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is this not basically the (putative) <code>setm</code> tactic you're talking about?</p>",
        "id": 600330398,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1780602168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I made a prototype of a <code>let_subterm</code> with <code>conv</code>-style syntax <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/Rob23oba/50b63ad729f6b2d9bb474edc3256dd3f\">here</a>. In contrast to <code>setm</code>, where specify a pattern for the goal, <code>let_subterm</code> lets you write a <code>conv =&gt; enter [...]</code> path. But instead of using <code>conv =&gt; enter [...]</code>, it has its own handling for those type of paths that allows it to reach any subexpression. Here's an example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: unsolved goals</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">a : Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">x : Nat → Nat := fun k =&gt; 4 * k</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">ty : Type := Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">q : Nat → Nat := fun k =&gt; k ^ 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">y : ty → Nat := fun k =&gt; q k + x k</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">z : Nat → Nat := fun k =&gt; y k + 4</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">b : Nat :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  match a with</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  | 0 =&gt; a ^ 2 + 6 * a + 9</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  | k.succ =&gt; z k</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">d : Nat := 2 * (a != 0).toNat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">c : Nat := (a + 3 - d) ^ 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ b = c</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value_of</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">let_subterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value_of</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Also, fun fact, did you know that <code>enter</code> has a <code>enter [in pattern]</code> syntax that <em>does literally nothing</em>?</p>",
        "id": 600526406,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780615004
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a general solution which allows you to forget the subterm from context using both set and generalize.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">enter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">clear</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This approach allows you to choose the subterm by focusing it with conv and then forget the definition of the subterm so that it doesn't clutter your context.</p>",
        "id": 601210513,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780941306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a way to collapse a hypothesis in the InfoView in VSCode? That would be a better solution to this problem.</p>",
        "id": 601210953,
        "sender_full_name": "Jesse Slater",
        "timestamp": 1780941413
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, it's the setting hide let values.</p>",
